  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_1">
    <text>Many materials can be used to craft different items.\nRecipes and manuals bought or found during your expeditions may contain a lot of crafting information.\nSelect a category in the crafting menu to see the items you can craft.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_2">
    <text>Select the item you want to craft.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_3">
    <text>The listed components are required to craft the selected item.\nIf the minimum amount of a component is missing, it will be highlighted in red and prevent crafting.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_4">
    <text>You have all the components needed to craft the selected item. Click “Craft” to continue.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_5">
    <text>There is no information yet on how to craft the selected item.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_6">
    <text>Crafting the selected item at this workbench requires “%s”.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_intro">
    <text>Many materials can be used to craft different items.\nRecipes and manuals bought or found during your expeditions may contain a lot of crafting information.\nSelect a category in the crafting menu to see the items you can craft.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_solution_2">
    <text>Manuals and recipes can provide information on crafting the selected item.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_solution_3">
    <text>These tools are usually rare, so keep an eye out during your expeditions.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_solution_4">
    <text>Components can be obtained by dismantling unwanted items and equipment.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_tip_1">
    <text>Select the item you want to craft.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_tip_5">
    <text>You have all the components required to craft “%s”. Click “Craft” to continue.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_warning_2">
    <text>There is no information yet on how to craft “%s”.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_warning_3">
    <text>Crafting the selected item from the listed components requires “%s” (available only from the player or a technician).</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_craft_warning_4">
    <text>Some components required to craft the selected item are missing from the inventory.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_1">
    <text>Damaged weapon or equipment parts can be replaced using spare parts and the appropriate tool kit.
Select the piece of equipment you want to repair from your inventory.\n</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_2">
    <text>Each piece of equipment has its own set of parts and materials.\nGray parts indicate that no suitable replacement is available in the inventory.\nIf you have a compatible part and “%s”, click the part you want to replace.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_3">
    <text>You can select an identical spare part from your inventory.\nReplacement parts must be in as good or better condition than the installed parts.\nGray parts are in worse condition than the parts already installed.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_4">
    <text>The parts are ready to install. Click “Repair” to install them.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_intro">
    <text>Damaged weapon or equipment parts can be replaced using spare parts and the appropriate tool kit.
Select the piece of equipment you want to repair from your inventory.\n</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_solution_1">
    <text>Parts can be obtained by dismantling weapons and equipment.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_solution_2">
    <text>Most technicians sell these kits. They can also be found in other ways.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_solution_3">
    <text>Some tools (Multitool, Cleaning Rod, File, Simple Sewing Thread, and Field Sewing Kit) let you repair parts using identical spares. Most technicians sell these tools, and they can also be found in other ways.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_tip_1">
    <text>Each piece of equipment has its own set of parts and materials.\nGray parts indicate that no suitable replacement is available in the inventory.\nIf you have a compatible part and “%s”, click the part you want to replace.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_tip_3">
    <text>You can select an identical “%s” spare part from your inventory.\nReplacement parts must be in as good or better condition than the installed parts.\nGray parts are in worse condition than the parts already installed.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_tip_4">
    <text>The parts are ready to install. Click “Repair” to install them.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_warning_1">
    <text>There are no parts in the inventory for the selected piece of equipment.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_warning_2">
    <text>“%s” is required to replace parts.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_repair_warning_3">
    <text>The “%s” part in the inventory is in worse condition than the installed part.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_state_1">
    <text>At the workbench, you can repair, upgrade, and craft items using the appropriate repair kits and tools.\nThe main tools available for this workbench are shown above. They let you repair, upgrade, and craft equipment.\nSelect one of the tabs to continue.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_ui_workshop_info_state_intro">
